---
/**
 * terms.astro — Terms of Service Page
 * Full terms with acceptable use, disclaimer, contact details.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — FreeFileTools"
  description="Read the Terms of Service for using FreeFileTools browser-side file conversion utilities. Covers acceptable use, disclaimers, and limitation of liability."
>
  <article class="page-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Last updated: August 2026 · By using FreeFileTools, you agree to these terms.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="page-body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing and using FreeFileTools ("the Website," "the Service"), you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms") and our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree to any part of these Terms, you must immediately discontinue use of the Website.
        </p>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. Continued use of the service following any changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p>
          FreeFileTools is a free, browser-based utility that allows users to convert, compress, and transform image files entirely within their own web browser. No files are uploaded to any remote server. All processing occurs locally using standard browser APIs including HTML5 Canvas, WebAssembly, and the File API.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Service is provided free of charge to individual users and organisations for both personal and commercial use, subject to the acceptable use terms below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You agree to use FreeFileTools only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Service to process, convert, or distribute files containing illegal, harmful, defamatory, obscene, or otherwise objectionable content.</li>
          <li>Attempt to reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or tamper with any portion of the Website or its source code.</li>
          <li>Use automated bots, scrapers, or scripts to access or interact with the Service in a manner that could damage, disable, overburden, or impair the infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Circumvent any security measure or access restrictions applied to the Website.</li>
          <li>Use the Website to infringe any intellectual property rights of any third party.</li>
          <li>Misrepresent your identity or affiliation with any person or entity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to restrict access to the Service for any user who violates these Acceptable Use terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          All content, branding, design, logos, source code, and written material on FreeFileTools are the intellectual property of FreeFileTools and its contributors. You may not reproduce, redistribute, or commercially exploit any part of the Website without explicit written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          The files you process using our tools remain entirely your own. We assert no ownership over any files, images, or data that you convert using the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Implied warranties of merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose.</li>
          <li>Guarantees that file conversions will be completely error-free, accurate, or uninterrupted.</li>
          <li>Warranties regarding the accuracy, completeness, or reliability of converted output files.</li>
          <li>Guarantees that specific image formats (such as AVIF) will be supported by every browser.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You use the Service entirely at your own risk. We strongly recommend keeping originals of all files you process.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, FREEFILETOOLS AND ITS DEVELOPERS, CONTRIBUTORS, PARTNERS, OR AFFILIATES SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages.</li>
          <li>Loss of data, revenue, profits, business opportunity, or goodwill.</li>
          <li>Damages resulting from conversion errors, file corruption, or output quality loss.</li>
          <li>Damages arising from your reliance on any output generated by the Service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Because all file processing takes place locally within your own web browser and no data is transmitted to our servers, FreeFileTools has no control over your local computing environment, browser compatibility, or the integrity of any file output.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Third-Party Services &amp; Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          FreeFileTools displays advertisements provided by third-party networks including Google AdSense. These third parties have their own privacy policies and terms of service which govern their use of your data. We recommend reviewing those policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party links or embedded content are provided for convenience only. We do not endorse, control, or accept responsibility for any third-party content, products, or services.
